%I A398569 #18 Aug 18 2026 18:19:53
%S A398569 315,495,525,585,693,735,765,819,825,855,975,1035,1071,1197,1275,1287,
%T A398569 1305,1395,1425,1449,1617,1665,1683,1725,1815,1827,1845,1881,1911,
%U A398569 1925,1935,1953,1989,2115,2175,2223,2275,2277,2325,2331,2385,2499,2535,2541,2583
%N A398569 Odd numbers of the form p^2*s, where p is prime, s is squarefree, gcd(p,s) = 1, and A001221(s) >= 2.
%C A398569 These are the odd terms of A398316. A398316 is the disjoint union of this sequence and A398787.
%C A398569 The asymptotic density of this sequence is (4/Pi^2) * Sum_{p odd prime} (1/(p*(p+1)) = A185199 * (A179119 - 1/6) = 0.0662896922512854770349... . - _Amiram Eldar_, Aug 10 2026
%H A398569 Michael De Vlieger, <a href="/A398569/b398569.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%F A398569 Numbers of the form p^2*q_1*q_2*...*q_r, where r >= 2, p,q_1,q_2,...,q_r are distinct odd primes.
%F A398569 Odd integers m such that A001221(m) >= 3 and A001222(m) = A001221(m) + 1.
%F A398569 Equals A398316 intersection A005408.
%F A398569 Equals (A072357 \ A054753) intersection A005408.
%e A398569 315 is a term because 315 = 3^2*5*7, so its prime-exponent signature is [1,1,2].
%e A398569 525 is a term because 525 = 3*5^2*7.
%e A398569 45 is not a term because 45 = 3^2*5 has only two distinct prime factors; it belongs to A398421.
%e A398569 225 is not a term because 225 = 3^2*5^2 has two prime exponents equal to 2 and is powerful. It belongs to A363217.
%t A398569 nn = 3200; s = Select[Range[1, nn, 2], And[PrimeNu[#] > 2, SquareFreeQ[#]] &]; Union@ Flatten@ Map[Function[{k, w}, Map[If[# < nn, #, Nothing] &[k*#] &, w]] @@ {#, FactorInteger[#][[;; , 1]]} &, s] (* _Michael De Vlieger_, Aug 10 2026 *)
%o A398569 (PARI) isok(k) = if(k == 1 || !(k % 2), 0, my(e = factor(k)[ ,2]); if(#e < 3, 0, e = vecsort(e, , 4); e[1] == 2 && e[2] == 1)); \\ _Amiram Eldar_, Aug 10 2026
%o A398569 (PARI) isok(k) = if ((k%2), my(f=factor(k), v=select(x->(x==2), f[,2], 1)); if (#v == 1, my(p=f[v[1],1], s=k/p^2); issquarefree(s) && (gcd(s,p) == 1) && (omega(s) >= 2))); \\ _Michel Marcus_, Aug 11 2026
%Y A398569 Cf. A001221, A001222, A054753, A398787.
%Y A398569 Cf. A179119, A185199.
%Y A398569 Subsequence of A005408, A072357, A360769, A391025, and A398316.
%Y A398569 A398421 consists of the odd minimal mixed composites with exactly two distinct prime factors; this sequence consists of those with at least three distinct odd prime factors.
%K A398569 nonn,new
%O A398569 1,1
%A A398569 _Charles Kusniec_, Aug 03 2026
